+Feature: Separate the lost per-run control path from established service
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:2: trailing whitespace.
+  Training rehearsal - synthetic data - not a live Azure result
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:3: trailing whitespace.
+  Source S089 / D-S089 / A-S089, frozen S unit in SC-S089.
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:4: trailing whitespace.
+  Connectivity, commands, routes, recovery and journeys are synthetic trace data.
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:5: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:6: trailing whitespace.
+  Background:
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:7: trailing whitespace.
+    Given an established blue-v1 route at synthetic epoch 7
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:8: trailing whitespace.
+    And an independent shared training harness that remains available
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:9: trailing whitespace.
+    And three fixed journeys with a 100 synthetic millisecond budget
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:10: trailing whitespace.
+    And at most six retained attempts and six events per attempt
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:11: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:12: trailing whitespace.
+  Scenario: Established routes do not require the controller on every request
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:13: trailing whitespace.
+    Given the independent fixture and confirmed recovery evidence
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:14: trailing whitespace.
+    When I prepare and lose only the per-run management path
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:15: trailing whitespace.
+    Then the synthetic management command is visibly rejected
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:16: trailing whitespace.
+    And the established route and epoch do not change
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:17: trailing whitespace.
+    When I sample the established journeys while management is unavailable
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:18: trailing whitespace.
+    Then attempted is 3, success is 3, failure is 0 and unknown is 0
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:19: trailing whitespace.
+    When the independent harness reports the fault and recovery acknowledgement
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:20: trailing whitespace.
+    Then data service is continuing, recovery is confirmed and verification is PASS
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:21: trailing whitespace.
+    And this is not a migrated-user or native-platform result
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:22: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:23: trailing whitespace.
+  Scenario: Requiring management on every request interrupts service
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:24: trailing whitespace.
+    Given the controller-dependent fixture
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:25: trailing whitespace.
+    When I lose management, sample, report and recover
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:26: trailing whitespace.
+    Then all three established journeys fail because they require the unavailable controller
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:27: trailing whitespace.
+    And a confirmed recovery cannot erase those failures
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:28: trailing whitespace.
+    And verification is FAIL even if my prediction correctly identifies the failure
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:29: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:30: trailing whitespace.
+  Scenario: An independent route can still have a real synthetic service error
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:31: trailing whitespace.
+    Given the service-error fixture
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:32: trailing whitespace.
+    When I lose management, sample, report and recover
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:33: trailing whitespace.
+    Then two journeys succeed and one fails with service-error
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:34: trailing whitespace.
+    And controller status is not used as a success-shaped data-plane fallback
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:35: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:36: trailing whitespace.
+  Scenario: Missing observations and missing recovery acknowledgements stay unknown
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:37: trailing whitespace.
+    Given the missing-sample fixture
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:38: trailing whitespace.
+    When I lose management, sample and report
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:39: trailing whitespace.
+    Then two journeys succeed and one is unknown, not a zero-latency success
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:40: trailing whitespace.
+    When confirmed recovery is observed
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:41: trailing whitespace.
+    Then the control path is available but data service remains unverified
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:42: trailing whitespace.
+    Given instead complete independent samples and missing recovery evidence
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:43: trailing whitespace.
+    When I lose management, sample, report and recover
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:44: trailing whitespace.
+    Then data service is continuing but control availability and recovery are unknown
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:45: trailing whitespace.
+    And verification is UNKNOWN, not claimed recovery
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:46: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:47: trailing whitespace.
+  Scenario: Fault reporting and recovery are independent of the lost run path
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:48: trailing whitespace.
+    When only the per-run management path is unavailable
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:49: trailing whitespace.
+    Then the shared harness can still report the scoped fault and its measured samples
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:50: trailing whitespace.
+    And only its fixed recovery evidence can confirm control restoration
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:51: trailing whitespace.
+    And no network, management or resource operation takes place
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:52: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:53: trailing whitespace.
+  Scenario: Strict inputs and ordered actions cannot mutate an invalid state
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:54: trailing whitespace.
+    Given an invalid enum, extra property, accessor, inherited record or wrong action order
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:55: trailing whitespace.
+    When I attempt an action
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:56: trailing whitespace.
+    Then it fails visibly before any state mutation
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:57: trailing whitespace.
+    And all actions enforce their exact parameter counts
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:58: trailing whitespace.
+    And returned snapshots and caller inputs cannot alter the internal lesson state
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:59: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:60: trailing whitespace.
+  Scenario: Retain negative and unknown attempts until explicit reset
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:61: trailing whitespace.
+    When I check a prediction and start a new attempt
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:62: trailing whitespace.
+    Then the full previous trace, samples, actual verdict and prediction remain
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:63: trailing whitespace.
+    And success plus failure plus unknown equals attempted in active and retained metrics
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:64: trailing whitespace.
+    And the seventh attempt is rejected without evicting history
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:65: trailing whitespace.
+    When I explicitly reset, including from a partial attempt
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:66: trailing whitespace.
+    Then all local state and history clear, defaults return and keyboard focus returns to the fixture
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:67: trailing whitespace.
+    And repeated reset is harmless
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:68: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:69: trailing whitespace.
+  Scenario: A portable keyboard lesson has an enforced offline surface
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:70: trailing whitespace.
+    Given the exact synthetic banner, source attribution, limits and disclaimer
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:71: trailing whitespace.
+    When I use native keyboard controls for the complete rehearsal
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:72: trailing whitespace.
+    Then phase guards, errors, outcomes and retained history are visible
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:73: trailing whitespace.
+    And reset does not shadow the native form reset method
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:74: trailing whitespace.
+    And narrow layout remains usable
learning/S089/evidence/red/outage.feature.snapshot:75: trailing whitespace.
+    And CSP blocks inline execution and connection attempts in the actual browser
